From e18869951a450c433155b8c7750116ead78d57b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:56:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix unpaid-order-to-kitchen, show all AU payment methods,
 independent admin nav scroll
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1) Unpaid orders no longer reach the kitchen. App checkouts create the Square
   order before charging, so a declined/abandoned payment (e.g. Apple Pay that
   never went through) was still cooked. App orders are now stamped bc_hold='1'
   and hidden from the KDS until /api/pay confirms payment and clears the flag.
   The KDS also shows any held order that has a payment tender or has settled, so
   a paid order is never lost even if the release step fails. A 15-min sweep
   cancels held orders that were never paid so they don't linger in Square.

2) Every Square-AU payment method is offered at checkout: the one-tap wallets
   (Apple Pay, Google Pay, Afterpay) now show even when a saved card is the
   current choice — previously they were hidden for returning customers — so
   card, wallets and gift balance are all selectable. (Cash App Pay / ACH are
   US-only and not applicable in AU.) Wallets stay hidden only where the sheet
   amount could differ from the charge (coupon/reward) or for scheduled orders.

3) Admin nav scrolls independently on iPad. On landscape (>=960px) the sticky
   nav had no height bound, so a nav taller than the short viewport could only be
   reached by scrolling the whole page — which a long section like Locations made
   impossible. The nav now has its own bounded, independently-scrollable height
   with overscroll containment.

